WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
{ED}

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.960
Good morning, boys and girls!

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.930
The whole world is standing by for your awakening! {The whole world is just waiting for you to get up!}{TLC: Magenta's the tokusatsu guy, so check, but sug. something like "The whole world is standing by for your awakening!" for a more dramatic tone (The Japanese is talking about getting up in the morning as if it were the awakening of heroic good children)}

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.400
Now rise, brave young boys and girls!

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.700
Yayoi! Time to get up!

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.690
Gimme a bit, Mom...

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:22.630
I made your favorite hotcakes for breakfast!

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:23.840
Hotcakes?!

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.770
Good morning, Mom!

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.720
Good morning!

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.070
Huh? Where are the hotcakes?

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:34.090
I'm sorry! But, you know, today is April 1st and all...

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:38.980
Oh, right! It's April Fools today, so it's alright to lie!

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:41.860
As long as you admit you're lying afterwards, of course!

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.630
Well, of course!

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.340
By the way, Mom...

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.470
I got myself a boyfriend. {Editor: That's just wrong Yayoi... Don't say that... not even jokingly... Now go get yourself a nice girlfriend...}

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:51.640
What?!

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.630
Just kidding!

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.040
You're so easily fooled.{TLC: ellipsis doesn't improve the script here.  Heads up to Ed: there are a few in the script that are like this (most are okay, it's just a few). I'll focus on TLC.}

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.740
Jeez, Yayoi!

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.510
And now we're even!

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:04.990
<i>Alright... I'd better make the most of this while I can!</i>

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.410
Smile! Smile! Smile! Smile!

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.240
Smile Precure!

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.140
Let's go!

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.680
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.810
All together!

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.410
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.620
Jump to tomorrow!

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.290
Smile Precure!

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:26.120
Smile! Smile! Smile Precure!

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:31.560
A smile, shining like the sun.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.770
We all carry an undying sparkle.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.710
Keep going with all you've got, girls!

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:47.650
Those beads of sweat are diamonds.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.610
So bright!

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:52.820
The future that you'll shine the way to

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:59.260
When five lights seize the will to win.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.760
Happy! Sunny! Peace! March! Beauty!

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:00.930
Let's go!

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.630
(Smile! Smile!) The power of a smile

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.560
(Smile! Smile!) Joins us all together.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.370
We'll never let a friend cry!

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:11.940
Girls! Let's go!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.600
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.740
Everybody!

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:16.410
Smile! Smile! Precure!

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.940
Fly to the future!

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.450
Sparkle! Smile Precure!

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.620
Smile! Smile! Smile! Smile!

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.920
Smile Precure!

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.210
How's that?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.130
Well, isn't this a rare surprise-dawasa?

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.810
Don't tell me you're breaking into the world of art?

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.930
It's April Fools today, after all-oni!

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.600
You know the tale of Momotarou, where he fights the oni?

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.900
I'm gonna rewrite it for the kids so the oni wins-oni!

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.820
What's the point of that?

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.910
We're going to give their world a Bad End anyway.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:55.870
So, the version where the oni wins will become the actual story.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.250
Wait... So my lie will be real, and reality will be a lie...?

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.740
I don't get it-oni!

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.790
You stupid wolf! Why'd you have to go confuse him like that?!

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.920
Whatever! My point is that lies rock-oni!{TLC: sug. a "Whatever!" "Anyway," at the beginning}

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:13.880
I'm gonna use my lies to make life miserable for those humans-oni!

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:28.070
Good morning, Miyuki-chan!

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.050
Morning, Yayoi-chan!

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.940
Good morning-kuru!

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:39.180
Hey, listen! My mom bought some donuts yesterday, and guess what? Candy ate them all!

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.180
<i>Oh, right! Today's April Fools!</i>

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.300
<i>Let's surprise Miyuki-chan a bit, shall we...?{TLC: "scare"->"surprise" is probably makes more sense. It's an April Fool's prank, not a Halloween's one.}</i>

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.250
Yayoi-chan?

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.010
Huh?

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.440
What's the matter?

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.240
Umm, Miyuki-chan...

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.120
There's something I've been meaning to tell you...

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.220
Huh? What's up?

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.280
I'm...

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.090
What's the matter-kuru?

00:03:56.070 --> 00:04:00.070
I'm... moving away!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.370
What?! Seriously?! {Uhhhm... If they're both saying this... How do I add in the -kuru anyways?}

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.440
<i>Gotcha! Fooled you good!</i>

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.240
When are you leaving...?

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:07.810
Huh?

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.910
<i>Guess a bit more won't hurt...</i>

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:15.240
Well, it's a bit sudden for me too, but... tomorrow...

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:16.880
Tomorrow?!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:21.130
<i>This is so much fun! But I guess I should tell her the truth...</i>

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:22.900
Guess what? I was joking!{TLC: sug. "Ha!  Just kidding!" (feels more like something we say in English)}

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.990
It's April Fools, see, so I thought I'd trick you and...

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.430
Huh?

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.030
Miyuki-chan...?

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:31.500
Akane-chan!

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.330
Oh! Mornin', Miyuki!

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.260
Now's not the time! I've got bad news! Okay, so...{TLC: sug. "Okay, so..."->"Listen up!" "Listen to this!"}

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:39.640
What is it?

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.640
You serious?! Yayoi's leavin' us?!

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.330
Akane!

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.240
Oh crap!

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.580
What are we gonna do?!

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.440
Okay, calm down, calm down!

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.820
First up, we gotta keep this secret!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.520
Secret? Why...?

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.660
Yeah, why-kuru?

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.560
Listen, I've been where she is. I know how she's gotta be feelin'.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.180
You do too, right, Miyuki?

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.630
Oh... right.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.000
I've gotta tell Miyuki-chan it was all a joke{ before she}...{TLC: "I've gotta hurry and tell Miyuki it was all a joke!" (The Japanese isn't a complete sentence, but it's a standard, well-known structure.  The Japanese listeners just hear the TL I just gave.)}

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:15.130
There she is!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.170
Hey, Yayoi-chan!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:19.350
G-Good mornin', Yayoi!

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.950
Good morning, Akane-chan!

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.480
Miyuki-chan, about what I said earlier...

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:24.740
I'm not-

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.820
Don't worry 'bout it, Yayoi!

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.840
Miyuki told me all about it.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:30.790
You're leavin' us, huh?

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:31.660
What?!

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:34.760
I'm sorry! I couldn't just keep it to myself.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.150
No, listen to me! I'm not-

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.510
Shush now, it's alright. I've been there.

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:42.710
I had trouble tellin' my friends when I had to leave 'em, too.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.070
Me too, actually.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.400
No, see...!

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:49.570
I know how you feel! A girl's always gonna have her troubles!{TLC: sug. "I know how you feel!" at the beginning.  Something feels missing otherwise, and it works better as a phrase for interrupting someone, anyway}

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:53.930
It's always the same! You find out, and you try and keep it all bottled up...

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.050
Makes you feel really lonely, doesn't it?

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:57.020
Poor Yayoi-kuru...

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.910
No, really! I was just-

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:00.570
Ya don't gotta say a thing!

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:01.990
It'll be alright!

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:05.190
We're here if you need us, Yayoi-chan!

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.380
Listen, everything I said before was-

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:09.220
Come on! Get in class!

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:11.060
Homeroom's about to begin.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.370
Yes, ma'am! {Sounds like normal speech to use ma'am.}

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.260
We'll talk to ya later, okay? Come on.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:19.240
<i>I've gotta tell them, before this gets any worse... {Editor: Is it just me or does Yayoi look like she has to pee?}</i>

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.730
Well then, that concludes our homeroom for today.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.430
I'll leave you to get ready for first period.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:31.260
Hey, Nao. Gotta talk to you about somethin'...

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.290
What?!

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.120
Oh my!

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:49.630
Miyuki-chan, Akane-chan, listen... about what we talked about this morning...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:50.820
Yayoi-san...

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:53.990
Akane has told me everything.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:57.270
Why didn't you tell us sooner?

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.320
About what?

00:06:58.320 --> 00:06:59.480
You leaving!

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:01.680
How do you two know about-?!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.540
You could have just talked to us about it, you know?!{TLC: I prefer "You could've told us!  There was no need to be shy!"}

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.660
Look, let's just not talk about it, okay?

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.370
Yeah! It'd be even harder to talk about it with her friends, right?

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:12.830
Right, Yayoi?

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.110
Yeah...

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:18.030
<i>Wait, what am I saying?! I've gotta tell them it was all a joke! {RL: Seriously Yayoi? do you have to go in a different way or something? Going to transform into Cure Peece?}</i>

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.730
How does that make it harder?

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:26.740
Think about it. If she talks about it to us, then the fact she's gonna have to say goodbye sinks in.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:33.060
Better to keep things normal as long as you can, and enjoy the time you have left together.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.800
Right, Yayoi-chan?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.800
Right...

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:38.690
<i>What am I doing?!</i>

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.810
It is a most saddening tale...

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.070
I didn't...

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:45.690
I'm sorry, Yayoi-chan. I can't imagine how hard this is for you...

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:47.520
It's alright, really...

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:50.830
<i>Oh god, I'm just making this even worse!</i>

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:53.850
Anyway, hadn't we better get to music class?

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:55.160
Indeed we should.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.770
We'll meet up and talk during our next free period, alright?

00:07:58.770 --> 00:07:59.340
Okay.

00:08:00.490 --> 00:08:03.810
<i>If this keeps up, then I'll become just a regular liar!</i>

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:13.260
I've gotta tell them the truth...

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.010
Even if they do get mad at me...

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.510
Cheer up, Yayoi-chan!

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:20.390
Are you worried about abandoning your Precure duties?

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.650
My Precure duties?

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.600
You were lookin' at your Smile Pact, right?

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.200
Oh, I was just...

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:32.820
Working together, as the five Precure, we've managed to persevere through these hardships...

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.750
But I fear...

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.110
Oh! I didn't even think we'd be down a member...

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.510
You feel bad about abandoning us, don't you?

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:41.520
B-But I'm not-

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.840
I know how you've gotta be feelin'!

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.990
But you won't solve anything by just frettin' over it alone!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.650
Don't worry about leaving the Precure, alright?

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.220
Huh?

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:58.050
We will do our best to cover for your absence.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:02.550
Even if we are separated, my thoughts will always be with you.

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:03.270
And mine!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.140
Mine too!

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:04.950
Don't forget me!

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.240
Or me-kuru!

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.710
<i>What am I gonna do?!</i>

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.100
Hey, where's Yayoi-chan?

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.400
Apparently she had something to take care of.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:20.020
I guess it'd be difficult for us to sit and eat together, what with all that's happenin'...

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:24.190
I have a proposal to run by you all.

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:33.140
I might not have the courage to tell them in person, but I can tell them through manga!

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:35.130
And done!{TLC: sug. "Finished!"}

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.110
Alright!

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.200
Now to show this to them, and...

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.380
Yayoi-chan!

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:50.740
So this is where you've been!

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:54.050
M-Miyuki-chan! What's the matter?

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.170
Let's Go: Blossom!

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:18.010
Any good little kids around?!

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.650
I've got a story to read to you about an oni beating the pulp out of Momotarou!

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.150
What's this-oni?

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:27.610
"I'm not really leaving! It was an April Fools' joke!"?

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.650
Peace!

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.530
Candy!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:46.560
I know you wanted to enjoy your remaining time here as normally as possible...

00:10:46.560 --> 00:10:51.390
As tough as it may be, we thought it would be best if we took this chance...

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:54.030
and wished you the best of luck in your future.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:56.080
N-No, see, I...

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.000
<i>This is seriously bad!</i> {RL: Seriously... Shouldn't she be standing in a puddle right now? :P }

00:10:58.550 --> 00:10:59.810
Yayoi-chan.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:05.000
This was all a bit sudden, Yayoi, so the only flowers I could get were the ones here at school...

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.340
But we're never...

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:07.710
gonna forget you, ya hear?

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:10.680
Umm... You see...

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.150
<i>Bad, really bad, mega bad! {RL: Well she's the yellow cure for a reason :P }</i>

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:15.890
And here are some farewell messages from us all.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.540
The thing is, I...

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:22.970
If you'd like to say a few words of farewell, Yayoi-san, then please go ahead.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:30.970
<i>If I admit I've been lying this whole time...</i>

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:34.070
If you think this counts as a white lie, you're sorely mistaken!

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:36.570
This isn't like you at all!

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.610
You've been takin' us all for fools!

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.410
I can't trust you anymore, Yayoi-chan...

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:43.020
Liar! {RL: That yellow circle isn't a spotlight :P }

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.390
The nerve of her!

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:46.180
<i>They'll be really mad... they'll all hate me...!</i>

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:49.730
<i>And nobody will talk to me anymore...</i>

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:52.360
<i>They wouldn't even let me be a Precure!</i>

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.530
You can do it, Yayoi-chan!

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.350
Don't cry, ya hear?

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:00.000
Be strong!

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.150
Yayoi-chan!

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:15.100
Yayoi-chan...

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:19.010
I'm terribly sorry. I went too far...

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:22.250
We weren't trying to upset you, but it looks like we did.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.050
It's our bad.

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:26.260
No... no, it's not!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.460
What a stupid drawing-oni!

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:31.930
I'll show them how brilliant lying really is-oni!

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:36.090
This world will be stained with the worst possible conclusion...

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:38.470
...a Bad End-oni!

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.700
The blank slate of your future will be clouded in darkness-oni!

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.080
Who cares about her, anyway?

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:49.580
Stupid farewell party...

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:59.580
The Bad Energy we gather from the humans will resurrect the Emperor of Darkness, King Pierrot-sama!

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:04.710
This again. {Previously missing line. Putting "This again" because Reika knows what's going on despite "Kore wa...?"}

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.800
We've gotta save them!

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.030
You're...!

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.830
Hurry and transform-kuru!

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:12.800
Yayoi-chan, you ready to go?

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:15.770
Yeah!

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:20.740
Ready?

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:24.060
Precure, Smile Charge!

00:13:24.060 --> 00:13:25.210
Go!

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.280
Go, go!

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.480
Let's go!

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.820
The light of the future, shining bright!

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.920
Cure Happy!

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.070
Dazzling sun!

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:42.990
Hot-blooded power!

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.660
Cure Sunny!

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.920
Rock, paper, scissors! Sparkling bright...

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.070
Cure Peace!

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:59.180
Laying down the gauntlet, with courage blazing!

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:02.320
Cure March!

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:08.230
A gentle heart as pure as the driven snow...

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:11.130
Cure Beauty!

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:15.730
Our five lights will blaze a path to the future!

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:25.900
Shining bright, Smile Precure!

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:31.640
There you are, Precure! This time, I'm taking you down for good-oni!

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.630
Come forth, Akanbe!

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:40.680
Akanbe!

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:42.690
Get them, Akanbe!

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:44.910
Akan... be!

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.760
Akanbe, punch them-oni!

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.460
Akan!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:52.700
Just kidding!{TLC: putting "Not!" out as another option}

00:15:56.590 --> 00:15:58.570
Now, roll them flat-oni!{TLC: sug. "roll them flat!" Rolling over is different.}

00:15:58.570 --> 00:15:59.870
Akan!

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.310
Just kidding!

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:06.310
You fell for it-oni!

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.280
What idiots-oni!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.350
Are you just gonna keep lying?!

00:16:11.750 --> 00:16:14.380
Ain't anyone told you lying won't get you anywhere?{the idiom the Japanese uses has no equivalent that I can think of and sounds hecka dumb literally. Nemui-chan, opinions? <3}{TLC: I know the pain :/ (literally it's "liars become thieves!") I tried to think of a phrase along the lines of "the devil makes work for idle hands" but I didn't come up with anything.}{Editor: Could we discuss this in the staff channel? It can't be that difficult but I'm not quite sure what I'm working with... I really need to learn Japanese faster >_>}

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:18.050
I really hate liars like you!

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:22.730
If you're going to challenge us, at least have the decency to fight fairly!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:27.640
Stupid girls! Lying is so much fun-oni!

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:30.220
Isn't that right, Cure Peace?

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:33.440
I saw your silly drawing!

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.540
That's the manga I drew!

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.610
Why would you want to apologize for lying, anyway-oni?

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:47.080
Lie as much as you want-oni! It's their fault for being deceived-oni!

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:48.180
Stop it!

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:50.650
Peace, what's he talking about...?

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:54.690
I think I'll have a good laugh at your pathetic friends buying into your lies-oni!

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:59.100
Don't you dare laugh at my friends!

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:01.400
What's he talking about?

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:04.300
Peace, if there's anything you have to say, just be honest...{Peace, you can tell us. Just be honest...}{TLC: Peace still hasn't been reassured that her friends will still respect her, so "Peace, if there's anything you've got to say, say it!", although that loses the "honest" link}

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.070
<i>Be honest...</i>

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:11.270
<i>But if I do, they're bound to hate me for it...</i>

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:16.250
It doesn't matter what you've done, Peace! I'll still like you! {Editor: I dunno, should we make it love instead of like for better yuri flow? :P}

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:21.670
You were the one who encouraged me when I first came here...

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:23.920
That made me so happy!

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.320
Happy...

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.540
I'm sorry! I've been lying to you all this whole time...

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:43.810
Lying...?

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:48.010
Yeah... I'm not actually moving away!

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:49.360
No way!

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.150
That was all a lie?!

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:56.510
It's April Fools today, so I thought I'd wind Miyuki-chan up a bit, so I just thought...{TLC: sug. dropping the "but then" and making it "so I just thought"}

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.050
I'm so, so sorry!

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.050
April Fools...?

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:01.610
Now you mention it...

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:02.990
That means you're allowed to lie, doesn't it?

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:04.540
Hey, Happy!

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.910
How could you fall for something like that?!

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:08.100
My bad!

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:13.660
But hey, Sunny, you were the one who kept saying you "knew how she's gotta be feelin'!" {RL: Lol why is Happy's tsun face so adorable?}

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:16.550
That's not really relevant here...{TLC: slightly libfag, but sug. "Now you're just getting into technicalities!" (literally, she's saying that the thing about her is just *different* from the thing about Miyuki. The classic transparent, hand-waving dismissal gag)}{Editor: Meh, I think it works better the way it is}

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.670
So you're not leaving...?

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:20.780
No, I'm not!

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:22.650
I don't ever wanna have to leave you!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.110
Thank goodness!

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:25.610
Hooray-kuru!

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:27.510
That is what's truly important.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:28.080
Yeah!

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.790
Then... you're not mad at me...?

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.920
What's there to get mad about?

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:35.930
If anything, it's all Happy's fault!{TLC: sug. "probably"->"all", since it's a joke (also, ellipsis to exclamation mark)}

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.500
We appreciate you being honest with us.{TLC: she would say "your being honest"}

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:39.260
We do!

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:44.530
I am so glad!

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:47.610
You big crybaby!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.610
Hey!

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.510
You done yet?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:55.810
Why are you getting so worked up over a little lie-oni?

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.380
Just get them, Akanbe!

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.080
Akanbe!

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:07.010
They've all been so kind to me, no matter what I've done...

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:10.930
That kindness gave me the courage I needed to tell the truth!

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:12.720
So what-oni?!

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:15.830
Akanbe, punch them!

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:18.600
Akan!

00:19:21.850 --> 00:19:23.170
Just kidding!

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:32.010
This made me realize... you should never tell a lie that makes people sad!{just how horrible it is to hurt someone with your lies!}{TLC: second part "you should never tell a lie that makes people sad!" (April Fool's jokes and white lies are still okay)}

00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:49.850
Precure...

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.600
Peace...

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.840
Thunder!

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:03.970
Akanbe...

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:13.570
This can't be happening! It's a lie! I can't lose-oni!

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:17.540
Huh...?

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:19.760
What have I...?

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:21.690
This is the Pudding Décor-kuru.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:24.780
Let's put it in the Decor Décor-kuru! {RL: Is it just me or did that whole theme make anyone else think Takanashi should have done the BGM on the op too?}

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.440
It was all a lie?!

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:31.640
I'm so, so sorry!

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:33.860
Wait, what?

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:35.410
You're not really leaving?

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:39.790
What Yayoi-chan said was just a little April Fools joke.

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:41.620
I guess I got a bit carried away.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:42.570
Yeah, you did!

00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:45.310
It was so obviously a joke, how did you take her seriously?!

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:47.320
We got all worked up for nothin'!

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:52.940
Says you! "Oh, I've been there, I know what it's like!"

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:58.490
Yayoi-san is most upset about causing all this trouble, too.

00:20:58.490 --> 00:20:59.940
You'll forgive her though, right?

00:21:00.310 --> 00:21:01.790
Huh, so what's why...

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.320
I thought it was a bit odd!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:05.320
Yeah, it's never <i>that</i> sudden!{TLC: I'm not sure about the naturalness.  "Yeah, it was too sudden!" is safer}{Edit: Hm? What's wrong with the way it already is?}

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:07.410
I'm glad you're staying with us, anyway!

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:11.180
Me too...

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:12.990
You're <i>ultra happy</i>, right?

00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:15.930
Yup! <i>Ultra happy</i> all the way!

00:21:15.930 --> 00:21:17.840
Just forget it, alright?

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.930
Hey, would you draw something for me?

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:21.520
Yeah, and me too!

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:24.260
Psst!

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:32.740
Still, though. It's hard not to hate you for what you did, Yayoi...

00:21:34.510 --> 00:21:35.900
I don't like it either...{TLC: long. "It's despicable!" (literally "I don't like it either", but that has the wrong nuance)}

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:39.580
I, too, must admit I find myself rather loathing you.

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:42.280
U-Uhh... me too!

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:48.050
Just kidding!

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:55.300
Which means we actually think the opposite! We all really like you, Yayoi!

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:55.960
Right!

00:21:57.010 --> 00:21:58.560
Jeez!

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:03.070
Now we're even!

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:46.040
You're running the shop, Akane-chan?

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:50.270
Well, our okonomiyaki joint'll be in trouble if I don't! Time to show my stuff!

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:52.790
Wow, Akane! Your okonomiyaki is really good!

00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:54.010
It really is!

00:23:54.010 --> 00:23:55.800
I want some too-kuru!

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:58.510
Still can't make it taste like my dad's, though...

00:23:58.510 --> 00:24:00.100
Ah, then he must have a secret ingredient!

00:24:00.100 --> 00:24:02.120
But what the heck could it be?!{TLC: sug. "is it"->"could it be"}

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:04.290
Smile Precure!

00:24:07.120 --> 00:24:09.410
Find your ultra happy smile!
